#
# Example of job definition:
# .---------------- minute (0 - 59)
# |    .------------- hour (0 - 23)
# |    |      .---------- day of month (1 - 31)
# |    |      |     .------- month (1 - 12) OR jan,feb,mar,apr ...
# |    |      |     |     .---- day of week (0 - 6) (Sunday=0 or 7) OR sun,mon,tue,wed,thu,fri,sat
# |    |      |     |     |
# *    *      *     *     *     command to be executed
#

# Automatic day/night, where the platform has a script that owns the switch.
# The guard is what makes this safe to keep in the shared crontab: on a platform
# with no such script the line costs one test and does nothing. Where the script
# does exist it still does nothing until the light thresholds are set, so this is
# inert on an uncalibrated camera too - see "daynight" for what to set.
* * * * * [ -x /usr/bin/daynight ] && /usr/bin/daynight cron
